# Bramwick, suspended, at Rook's table.
dialogue bramwick4
  node root bramwick "Fenn. You came back. Good. Cray asked me to write the Marrow down as lost, early. I said no. First time in three years."
    -> badly
  node badly bramwick "He had me suspended by supper. It's my first evening off in thirty years, and I'm spending it badly."
    > "Cray says you were suspended for conduct." if not seen:bramwick4.conduct -> conduct
    > "How do we get you reinstated?" if not seen:bramwick4.paper -> reg2
    > "The ledger's chained to its desk." if seen:bramwick4.paper and not ledger_taken -> chain
    > "Where would Cray keep his insurance books?" if seen:bramwick4.paper and not has claims_book -> counting
    > "Who would preside over an inquiry?" if seen:bramwick4.paper and not seen:bramwick4.preside -> preside
    > "Goodnight, sir." -> bye
  node hub bramwick "Still suspended, Fenn. Still spending it badly. Two drinks and an apology, and the apology went down worse."
    > "Cray says you were suspended for conduct." if not seen:bramwick4.conduct -> conduct
    > "How do we get you reinstated?" if not seen:bramwick4.paper -> reg2
    > "The ledger's chained to its desk." if seen:bramwick4.paper and not ledger_taken -> chain
    > "Where would Cray keep his insurance books?" if seen:bramwick4.paper and not has claims_book -> counting
    > "Who would preside over an inquiry?" if seen:bramwick4.paper and not seen:bramwick4.preside -> preside
    > "Goodnight, sir." -> bye
  node conduct bramwick "Conduct unbecoming. Saying no to Mr Cray is very unbecoming, it turns out. I'd forgotten how much I enjoy it."
    -> conduct2
  node conduct2 rook "He's told me nine times. The last three, he stood up."
  node reg2 bramwick "Regulation two, Fenn. A harbourmaster suspended by a party to fraud is reinstated on proof of the fraud."
    -> proof
  node proof bramwick "Proof. Not a story. Marta has stories. Paper, before the bell."
    > "What paper?" -> paper
  node paper bramwick "My ledger, with my own lie in it. Cray's insurance books. And a man who was there when it happened."
    note bramwick_paper "Regulation two: proof of Cray's fraud puts Bramwick back. Paper, before the bell: his ledger, Cray's insurance books, and a man who was there."
    -> look
  node look narrator "He doesn't look at Rook. Very carefully, he doesn't look at Rook."
  node chain bramwick "I chained it there myself. Regulation thirty-one: the ledger stays in the loft. I wrote that one. Can't think why. Bring something heavy."
  node counting bramwick "Cray & Co., up Chandler's Lane. Nothing leaves that office without a stamped requisition."
  node preside bramwick "Not me. I'm a party. Not Cray. He's the other party. Someone who owns a tavern and hates an unfinished story."
    -> presided
  node presided narrator "He looks at Marta. Marta finds something very interesting on the ceiling."
  node bye bramwick "Goodnight, Fenn. Don't let him write anyone down. Not tonight. Not ever, ideally."
  # After the inquiry, before he has his stamp.
  node after bramwick "Reinstated, Fenn. Regulation two. Regulation forty, which I wrote an hour ago. Never been so well regulated. My stamp, when you're ready."
  # Giving the stamp back (rooms_act4.ts): the quarantine comes down.
  node stamp narrator "I put the harbour stamp in his hand. He weighs it. He'd already decided it was lost."
    -> notice
  node notice narrator "“Notice to all shipping,” says Bramwick. He turns Cray's order over, writes on the back, and stamps it. QUARANTINE LIFTED."
    -> hate
  node hate bramwick "There. On the back of his own paper. He'll mind that more than the cell."
    -> boom
  node boom narrator "A boy runs it to the boom. The yellow flag comes down. A hundred and thirty people cheer. One of them, a little late, is my father."
    -> took
  node took marta "Took you long enough."
    -> crying
  node crying narrator "She's crying. Everyone in the Salty Keel can see she's crying."
    -> onions
  node onions marta "Nobody write that down."
    -> back
  node back narrator "He presses the stamp back into my hand."
    -> entry
  node entry bramwick "One entry still wants correcting, and it shouldn't be in my hand. Use it. Then bring it back. Clerks always bring them back."
    note the_entry "The flag is down. One entry in the harbour ledger still needs correcting, at the bar, in front of everyone. Bramwick won't write it in his own hand."
    -> fourteen
  node fourteen fenn "Regulation fourteen, sir. Any clerk of this house may stamp in the Harbourmaster's absence."
    -> absent
  node absent bramwick "I'm not absent, Fenn. I'm right here. (He turns to the window.) …Though I find the harbour very absorbing just now."
  # The IOU: talking to him once the quarantine is lifted.
  node debt bramwick "Fenn. I have a debt to settle, and I need a witness. Clerks make good witnesses. Nobody suspects them of feelings."
    > "The IOU in your drawer." if seen_iou -> read
    > "What debt?" if not seen_iou -> fished
  node read bramwick "You read it."
    > "Including the small writing." -> small
  node small bramwick "…Then you know what I owe."
    -> lay
  node fished bramwick "Thirty years it lived in my drawer. Cray dumped the drawer into a sack. I searched his rubbish tonight. Don't put that in the ledger."
    -> lay
  node lay narrator "He lays a creased slip on the bar. IOU, ONE GAME OF CARDS, UNPAID. Marta reads it. Then the small writing. She reads that twice."
    -> everything
  node everything marta "“And everything else.” Thirty years, you old fool."
    -> paying
  node paying bramwick "I'm paying it."
    -> shuffle
  node shuffle narrator "Marta takes a pack of cards from her apron pocket. It has been waiting there thirty years. She shuffles."
    -> hand
  node hand marta "One more hand. For the debt."
    -> else
  node else bramwick "And everything else?"
    set iou_paid
    -> deal
  node deal marta "Deal."
    > "You'd have found it right at the front of the drawer." if seen:tavernkeeper.front -> front
    > "Shall I keep score?" -> score
    > "(Leave them to it.)" -> END
  node front marta "Right at the front. I've thought about nothing else since you told me. Now get out, clerk, before I start liking you again."
  node score marta "Keep your nose out of it. That's what you'll keep. Thirty years I've waited to lose this one properly."
  # Afterwards, at cards.
  node cards bramwick "Shh, Fenn. I've a pair of threes, and this time it's a strategy."
